feat(rbac): phase 2b -- project members management (UI + endpoints)

Backend (new ai_qa_portal/backend/routers/memberships.py):
- GET    /api/projects/{name}/members           any project member
- POST   /api/projects/{name}/members            TL+ to add Member/Lead; PM+ to grant PM
- PATCH  /api/projects/{name}/members/{user_id}  PM+ only; rejects role=pm if caller isn't PM
- DELETE /api/projects/{name}/members/{user_id}  PM+ only
- Last-PM constraint: refusing to remove or demote the only PM (409). Caller must
  promote another PM first, or delete the project entirely.

Frontend:
- New page /projects/[name]/members:
  * Member list grouped/sorted PM > Lead > Member, with avatar + email + role chip.
  * Inline role dropdown (PM/Admin only) and Remove button (PM/Admin only).
  * Add-member form (TL+) with email + role; only PMs can grant PM in the dropdown.
  * "Your role on this project" header line.
- Hooks: new lib/useMe.ts -- SWR-cached /api/me with helpers
  membershipFor() and roleAtLeast() so any page can do role-aware UI without
  refetching.
- /projects page is now role-aware:
  * Hides "+ New Project" if me is null (auth disabled bypass remains).
  * Each project card shows the user's role chip (PM/Lead/Member).
  * Delete X icon now only renders for PMs of that project.
- /projects/[name] page gets a "Manage members ->" button next to the title.

Side effect: any user listed in /api/me.memberships includes the project_slug
they're a PM of, so future Phase 2c invitation UI can present "your projects"
without an extra fetch.

No destructive changes. AUTH_DISABLED=true users keep the synthetic-admin
behaviour and see the full UI.
